.TH LIBKECCAK_K12_CREATE 3 LIBKECCAK
.SH NAME
libkeccak_k12_create - allocate a streaming KT128 context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libkeccak/k12.h>

struct libkeccak_k12 *libkeccak_k12_create(void);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lkeccak .
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libkeccak_k12_create ()
function allocates and zero-initialises a new KT128 context ready to
accept message bytes through
.BR libkeccak_k12_update (3).
The context holds all of its working storage in one bounded allocation;
see
.BR libkeccak_k12 (7).
.SH RETURN VALUES
A newly allocated context is returned on success. On allocation failure
NULL is returned and
.I errno
is set by the underlying allocator.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libkeccak_k12_destroy (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12_update (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12 (7)
